LAB 4 – CONSUMER OFFSETS AND MESSAGE REPLAY

Duration: 25 minutes

We will use day5-retention rather than the short-retention topic.

Step 1: Start a consumer group

```bash
sudo docker exec -it kafka-day1 \
  /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-console-consumer.sh \
  --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \
  --topic day5-retention \
  --group day5-replay-group \
  --from-beginning
```

Let it consume the available records, then stop using Ctrl+C.

Step 2: Inspect committed offsets

```bash
sudo docker exec kafka-day1 \
  /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-consumer-groups.sh \
  --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \
  --describe \
  --group day5-replay-group
```

Step 3: Preview offset reset

Make sure the consumer group is inactive, then execute:

```bash
sudo docker exec kafka-day1 \
  /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-consumer-groups.sh \
  --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \
  --group day5-replay-group \
  --topic day5-retention \
  --reset-offsets \
  --to-earliest \
  --dry-run
```

This previews the proposed reset without applying it.

Step 4: Execute the reset

```bash
sudo docker exec kafka-day1 \
  /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-consumer-groups.sh \
  --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \
  --group day5-replay-group \
  --topic day5-retention \
  --reset-offsets \
  --to-earliest \
  --execute
```

Step 5: Replay records

```bash
sudo docker exec -it kafka-day1 \
  /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-console-consumer.sh \
  --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \
  --topic day5-retention \
  --group day5-replay-group
```

The consumer can read retained records again from the reset positions.

Critical Teaching Point

Resetting a consumer group's offsets does not restore deleted records.

Replay works only for records still retained in Kafka.

