LAB 4 – Write Kafka Streams Java Application

Step 1: Create Java file

Execute:

bash

```bash
nano src/main/java/com/training/OrderStreamApp.java
```

Copy the complete Java program:

java

```java
package com.training;

import java.util.Properties;

import org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.Serdes;
import org.apache.kafka.streams.KafkaStreams;
import org.apache.kafka.streams.StreamsBuilder;
import org.apache.kafka.streams.StreamsConfig;
import org.apache.kafka.streams.kstream.KStream;
import org.apache.kafka.streams.kstream.Produced;

public class OrderStreamApp {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Properties props = new Properties();

        props.put(
            StreamsConfig.APPLICATION_ID_CONFIG,
            "day6-order-stream-app"
        );

        props.put(
            StreamsConfig.BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS_CONFIG,
            "localhost:9092"
        );

        props.put(
            StreamsConfig.DEFAULT_KEY_SERDE_CLASS_CONFIG,
            Serdes.String().getClass()
        );

        props.put(
            StreamsConfig.DEFAULT_VALUE_SERDE_CLASS_CONFIG,
            Serdes.String().getClass()
        );

        StreamsBuilder builder = new StreamsBuilder();

        KStream<String, String> orders =
            builder.stream("day6-orders-input");

        KStream<String, String> processedOrders = orders
            .filter((key, value) -> value != null)
            .mapValues(value -> value.toUpperCase());

        processedOrders.to(
            "day6-orders-output",
            Produced.with(Serdes.String(), Serdes.String())
        );

        KafkaStreams streams =
            new KafkaStreams(builder.build(), props);

        Runtime.getRuntime().addShutdownHook(
            new Thread(streams::close)
        );

        streams.start();

        System.out.println(
            "Kafka Streams application started..."
        );
    }
}
```

Save:

- `Ctrl + O`
- `Enter`
- `Ctrl + X`

Verify Java file:

bash

```bash
cat src/main/java/com/training/OrderStreamApp.java
```

Step 2: Understand the Java application

Java Code Explanation for Students

| Java component | Explanation |
| --- | --- |
| Properties | Stores application configuration |
| APPLICATION\_ID\_CONFIG | Unique identifier for the Streams application |
| BOOTSTRAP\_SERVERS\_CONFIG | Kafka broker connection |
| StreamsBuilder | Builds the processing topology |
| KStream | Represents a continuous event stream |
| filter() | Removes records with null values |
| mapValues() | Converts message values to uppercase |
| to() | Writes processed records to output topic |
| KafkaStreams | Creates the Kafka Streams runtime |
| streams.start() | Starts continuous processing |
| streams.close() | Closes application gracefully |

Processing Flow

Input Topic

`day6-orders-input`

↓

KStream

Reads order events

↓

filter()

Removes null values

↓

mapValues()

Converts messages to uppercase

↓

Output Topic

`day6-orders-output`

Important teaching point: This application preserves each message's key while transforming its value.

Example:

text

```text
Input:
101:order created

Output:
101:ORDER CREATED
```

