Additional Interview Answers for Trainers

| Question | Short answer |
| --- | --- |
| What is Kafka Streams? | Java library for processing Kafka data streams |
| What is KStream? | Represents continuous events |
| What is KTable? | Represents latest keyed state |
| What is stateless processing? | Processing without maintaining state between records |
| What is stateful processing? | Processing that maintains information across records |
| What is a state store? | Local storage for processing state |
| What is windowing? | Grouping events into time-based windows |
| What is application ID? | Identifies a Streams application and its associated Kafka resources |
| What is fault tolerance? | Ability to recover from failures |
| What is exactly-once v2? | Transactional processing guarantee within Kafka's supported boundary |

