P103:PAYMENT SUCCESS
P104:PAYMENT PENDING
P105:PAYMENT SUCCESS
P106:PAYMENT FAILED

4. Expected Output

Your payment-output topic should contain only successful payment events.

text
P101:PAYMENT SUCCESS
P103:PAYMENT SUCCESS
P105:PAYMENT SUCCESS


Failed and pending payment events must not appear in the output topic.

5. Technical Requirements

Your Java application must use:

Properties for Kafka configuration.
StreamsBuilder to create the processing topology.
KStream to read payment events.
filter() to select successful payments.
mapValues() to convert messages to uppercase.
to() to publish processed messages.
KafkaStreams to start the application.
6. Submission Requirements

Submit the following screenshots:

Kafka input and output topic creation.
Java source code (PaymentStreamApp.java).
Maven compilation showing BUILD SUCCESS.
Kafka Streams application running successfully.
Payment events published to the input topic.
Processed payment events displayed from the output topic.

Also submit a short explanation of how your Kafka Streams application works.

